  "notes": "The research covers two decades and says the later work changes the kit, so this is two modes rather than an average. `premier-lineage` is the modest MPC swing the archetype is built on — 0.58, the classic setting — with a rimshot-layered snare and heavy ghosts. `live-kit` drops `quantizeStrength` to 0.7, opens the perc lanes to a full acoustic set and pushes ghost probability to 0.4, which is what \"layered live-sounding kits\" means in parameters. Jazz-inflected harmony throughout: i–iv and ii–V–i with `seventh` at 0.52, and \"low-to-medium note density\" as `densityPerBar` [2,6]. The bass walks — the research says \"filtered sample bass or replayed electric with walking motion\" — so it is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.5 with a five-interval passing-tone set. ⚠ The bare-`i` family at weight 2 is the 2-bar modal loop the research describes, not an invented progression. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this medium-high: the collaboration history is documented but the numbers come from the producer's documented method rather than from Royce's own sessions.",
